{"title":"Their Respective Reasons","synopsis":"Gravestone tries to kill each separated individual."},{"title":"Desert Folklore","synopsis":"Honoka takes a break from work by traveling in the desert with Millie and Iks."},{"title":"Fairy Visions","synopsis":"Millie was rescued by a fairy and wolf when attacked by a monster in the desert."},{"title":"Night of the Sandstorm","synopsis":"The group search for the fairy and the wolf. Honoka opposes Leon's search for the fairy and is almost killed."},{"title":"Life Dancing Wildly","synopsis":"Honoka is healed by Kamui the wolf. When they resume their search for the fairy, they encounter Leon again."},{"title":"Rona Fauna","synopsis":"Rona Fauna, one of Third, has seized control of the wormhole drive weapon and is holding Jouganki prisoner. Honoko has been asked to rescue him."},{"title":"Engage","synopsis":"Two unexpected individuals join Honoka’s rescue team."},{"title":"Breaking Through Enemy Lines","synopsis":"Honoka gets separated from Bogie and Paifu and has to join forces with Blue Breaker."},{"title":"Facing Down Death","synopsis":"Paifu and Bogie defeat their opponents. Rona Fauna becomes very weak from overusing her powers and becomes unable to control her powers."},{"title":"Emotions That Fall Short","synopsis":"Rona expresses her love for Jouganki and her jealousy for Honoka."},{"title":"The Mirage of a Soul Never to Return","synopsis":"Rona has a showdown with Honoka and the wormhole driver is activated to destroy the entire planet."},{"title":"To the Steel Gorge","synopsis":"Both Iks and Honoka for different reasons to head to the Steel Gorge and face the Third."},{"title":"The Story That Begins Here","synopsis":"Jouganki, Iks and Honoka go into the crevasse of the Steel Gorge to meet the Observer of the planet."}],"failure":null,"fields":{},"episodes":{}}
